! C22-6578 PROBLEM 4.13, "NUMERICAL INTEGRATION", printed pp.47-51 (PDF
! 48-52), Method 1 (the program is printed pp.49-50), read in the ink
! at 250 dpi.  THE LAST PROBLEM IN THE BOOK.
!
!   "Provide a subroutine to handle the numerical integration of any
!   function over any finite interval.  Use it to evaluate:
!   I = integral from 0 to 1 of 2x e**(e**-x) / sqrt(1 - e**-x) dx"
!
! The page's specification (c), printed p.48: LEGQ8 is entered by "LVI,
! $15, $+1.0;B, LEGQ8"; "the leading 19 bits of the ensuing full word
! must contain the address of the subroutine for the evaluation of the
! integrand"; then the lower limit A, the upper limit B, the error
! return at 3.0($15) and the normal return at 4.0($15) with "the
! approximate value of the integral ... in the accumulator".
!
! FOUR PRINTED PIECES, assembled together in the page's order (its
! arrangement (d), printed pp.48-49): MAIN, LEGQ8, SUBR, and EXP, which
! the page gives as "(identical with a previous program)" and is
! printed p.46 as decks/problem_4_11.strap has it, substitutes and
! errata included.  EVERY INSTRUCTION IS AS PRINTED.  The label is
! printed "Main" and the comment (a) calls it MAIN.
!
! SUBSTITUTED, two cards, for one cause: "DD(N), 0.0" (MAIN's lower
! limit, and LEGQ8Z) is refused by this assembler, a zero DD(N)
! (decks/repro_dd_n_zero.strap).  Each is "DD(BU,64,8), 0", a zero
! fraction with exponent 0.  The program needs only a zero fraction:
! DL(N) of it then D-(N) of 1.0 is -1.0 whatever the zero's exponent.
!
! WRONG IN THE INK, AND RUN AS PRINTED: LEGQ8X's fourth abscissa is
! printed ".18343 46434 95650".  The 8-point Legendre-Gauss node is
! .18343 46424 95650 -- the ninth digit is a 3 for a 2.  The other three
! abscissae and all four weights agree with the standard table to their
! fifteen printed digits.  The misprint is worth 5.3E-11 in the answer,
! about fifteen thousand units of its 48-bit fraction, so it is far
! above what the check resolves, and the check follows it: the expected
! value below is computed from the nodes AS ASSEMBLED.
!
! WHAT IS COMPUTED IS THE RULE, NOT THE INTEGRAL.  With a = 0, b = 1:
!
!   G = 1/2 * sum over the four z, w of
!           w * ( f(1/2 + z/2) + f(1/2 - z/2) )
!     = 2.72454650263146   with the nodes as printed
!       2.72454650268418   with the fourth node corrected
!   I = 2.72362017099      the integral itself
!
! The integrand goes as 2e sqrt(x) at 0, so the 8-point rule is good to
! three figures and no more (the page's comment (d): exact for
! polynomials of 15th degree or less; (e): "in case of suspicion of
! inaccuracy, the domain can be subdivided").  ANS is checked against G.
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES THAT 4.11 AND 4.12 DID NOT, by the Reference
! Manual:
!   SIC, SUBR; NOP     a word of DATA written as instructions: LVE, $2,
!                      0.($15) takes the effective address of the half
!                      word at 0.($15) without executing it (printed
!                      p.29), and the two SVA store it into the address
!                      fields of "B, $" at LEGQ8A and LEGQ8B (p.24).
!                      THE PROGRAM MODIFIES ITSELF, and the check reads
!                      both words back.
!   DL / D- / E-I(U)   -(b-a)/2;  SRD(N), LEGQ8P stores it ROUNDED
!                      (printed p.96);  D+ b;  SRD(N), LEGQ8Q.
!   LFT / *N+ / *+     LOAD FACTOR then MULTIPLY AND ADD: Q -+ P z, the
!                      argument, formed double-length in one step
!                      (printed pp.98-99).
!   D* W, D+ T, D+ S, ST(N) S, SLO(U) T
!                      the sum is kept in TWO words, high and low: SLO
!                      stores accumulator bits 60-107 as a word of its
!                      own (printed p.97).
!   *N(N), LEGQ8P      times -P = (b-a)/2.
!   SX / LX of $2, $15 saved and restored through LEGQ82 and LEGQ8F.
!
! EXPECTED RESULTS ARE WORKED FROM THE PAGE, NOT THE MODEL
! (tests/verify_problem_4_fp.py 4.13, sixty-digit decimal arithmetic):
!
!   within a bound
!     ANS     G as above, twice as in 4.11: within 8 units of the 48-bit
!             fraction of G with EXP taken as 2**(x * RLN2), and within
!             16 of G with a true e**x.  Every argument is between 0 and
!             1, so EXP's 1.39 |x| is under a unit and a half per call,
!             and 4.12 measured one f at 2.3 units; eight of them, each
!             weighted by under .19, into a double-length sum.
!             THE LOW BITS ARE NOT PINNED.
!   exact, by hand
!     the halt   the BEW after "ST(U), ANS", MAIN + 5.32, not the error
!                BEW at MAIN + 4.0.
!     LEGQ8P     -(b - 0)/2, b the printed "DD(N), 1.0".  STRAP II makes
!                that 10 x (1/10 truncated) = .FFFFFFFFFFFF x 2**0, one
!                unit below 1 (C22-6729 pp.108-111; docs/NEXT.md "DD(N)
!                1.0 IS 1 - 2^-48"); E-I halves it exactly and SRD has
!                no bit 49 to round: .FFFFFFFFFFFF x 2**-1, negative =
!                003F FFFF FFFF FFF8.
!     LEGQ8Q     (b + 0)/2 = 003F FFFF FFFF FFF0.
!                (Until 2026-11-16 the deck ran on an exact 1.0 and these
!                were 0008 0000 0000 0008 and 0008 0000 0000 0000.)
!     $2         0, as it was: LEGQ8 "restored during exit".
!     $15        MAIN + 1.0 in the value field, as MAIN's LVI left it.
!     LEGQ82, LEGQ8F   the saved $2 and $15, the same two words.
!     LEGQ8A, LEGQ8B   the word holding each "B, $", with that half
!                word reading "B, SUBR" -- the same deck assembled with
!                "B, SUBR" written there.
!     $14        value 14.0, count 0, refill XW14 (EXP's, as in 4.11).
!
! OBSERVED INJECTIONS, 2026-11-15, each
!   python3 tests/verify_problem_4_fp.py 4.13 --sub OLD NEW
! with one data card changed.  Control: 9 exact checks and the PC pass,
! 2 within-bound checks pass, ANS = 004A E5EF 84B4 EEC0 =
! 2.72454650263143, off 2.11 units from the program's number and 2.04
! from the rule's.
!
!   the upper limit 1.0 -> 2.0
!       FAILED: P and Q (0028..08 and 0028..00, -1 and 1) and both ANS
!       checks (6.99).  Nothing else.
!   SUBR's WON 1.0 -> 1.00000000001
!       FAILED: both ANS checks, off 3572 units, and only those.
!   LEGQ8I's count, "XW, 0,4,$" -> "XW, 0,3,$"
!       FAILED: both ANS checks (1.67: the fourth node pair is missing).
!   the misprinted node corrected, ".18343 46434 95650" -> "...46424..."
!       PASSED, AS IT SHOULD: ANS moved to 004A E5EF 84B5 D6A0 =
!       2.72454650268415 and the expected value moved with it, off 2.18
!       units.  The model follows a node changed in its ninth digit.
!   the fourth weight's twelfth digit, "78362" -> "79362"
!       PASSED likewise, off 1.96 units: the oracle reads the data.
!   SUBR's WON 1.0 -> 1.00000000000001 (one part in 1E14)
!       SURVIVED, off 5.11 units against 8.  The floor, as in 4.12.

        SLC, 1000.0
! Main program for numerical integration.  Answer should be in ANS.
MAIN    LVI, $15, $+1.0; B, LEGQ8
        SIC, SUBR; NOP
! printed: DD(N), 0.0                   'lower limit
        DD(BU,64,8), 0
        DD(N), 1.0                      !upper limit
        BEW, $; NOP                     !error measure
        ST(U), ANS; BEW, $              !normal end of program
ANS     DRZ(U), (1)
! 8-point Legendre-Gauss integration subroutine
! integrand evaluation subroutine with 1.($15) return must be provided by user, with
!   effective address at 0.($15), lower limit must be at 1.($15) and upper limit at
!   2.($15), both as floating-point numbers.
! the integration subroutine will return normally at 4.($15), with answer in $L.
! error return is 3.($15).
LEGQ8   SX, $2, LEGQ82;SX,$15,LEGQ8F
        LVE,$2,0.($15)
        SVA, $2, LEGQ8A
        SVA, $2,LEGQ8B
        DL(N), 1.($15)
        D-(N), 2.($15)                  !a-b
        E-I(U),1                        !-(b-a) /2
        SRD(N),LEGQ8P
        D+(N), 2.($15)                  !(b+a)/2
        SRD(N),LEGQ8Q
        LX, $2, LEGQ8I;L(U),LEGQ8Z
        ST(U), LEGQ8S;ST(U), LEGQ8T
LEGQ8L  DL(U), LEGQ8Q
        LFT(U), LEGQ8P
        *N+(N), LEGQ8X($2)              !(b-a) z/2 + (b+a) /2
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
LEGQ8A  B, $                            !branch address changeable
        B, LEGQ8E; NOP                  !error
        ST(N), LEGQ8R                   !normal return from integrand subroutine
        DL(U), LEGQ8Q
        LFT(U), LEGQ8P
        *+(N), LEGQ8X($2)               !-(b-a) z/2 + (b+a) /2
        LVI, $15, $+1.0
LEGQ8B  B, $                            !branch address changeable
        B, LEGQ8E; NOP
        +(N), LEGQ8R
        D*(N), LEGQ8W($2)
        D+(N), LEGQ8T
        D+(N), LEGQ8S
        ST(N), LEGQ8S
        SLO(U), LEGQ8T
        CB+, $2, LEGQ8L
        *N(N), LEGQ8P
        LX, $2, LEGQ82                  !normal return to main program
        LX, $15, LEGQ8F
        B, 4.0($15)
LEGQ8E  LX, $2, LEGQ82
        LX, $15, LEGQ8F
        B, 3.0($15)
LEGQ82  XW, 0                           !changeable
LEGQ8F  XW, 0                           !changeable
! printed: LEGQ8Z DD(N),0.0
LEGQ8Z  DD(BU,64,8), 0
LEGQ8I  XW, 0,4,$
LEGQ8R  DR(N), (3)
LEGQ8S  SYN(N), LEGQ8R+1.0
LEGQ8T  SYN(N), LEGQ8R+2.0
LEGQ8P  DR(N), (1)
LEGQ8Q  DR(N), (1)
LEGQ8X  DD(N), .96028 98564 97536, .79666 64774 13627
        DD(N), .52553 24099 16329, .18343 46434 95650
LEGQ8W  DD(N), .10122 85362 90376, .22238 10344 53374
        DD(N), .31370 66458 77887, .36268 37833 78362
! end of LEGQ8 subroutine
! SUBR is a bona fide subroutine with 0($15) error exit and normal return 1.0($15).
SUBR    SX, $15, SAVE15
        ST(N), SAVEX
        LN(N), SAVEX
        LVI, $15, $+1.0;B, EXP          !go to EXP subroutine
        B, ERR; NOP
RTURN   ST(U), TEMP
        LVI, $15, $+1.0;B, EXP          !go to EXP subroutine
        B, ERR; NOP
        *(N), SAVEX
        E+I(U), 1
        ST(U), SAVEX                    !2*X*e**e**-X
        LN(U), TEMP
        +(N), WON
        SRT(N), $L                      !square root of 1-e**-x
        R/(N), SAVEX
        LX, $15, SAVE15; B, 1.0($15)    !normal return
ERR     LX,$15, SAVE15; B,0.0($15)      !error return
WON     DD(N), 1.0
SAVE15  XW, 0
SAVEX   DR(N), (1)
TEMP    DR(N), (1)
! EXP subroutine
! (identical with a previous program)
! ---- printed p.46, Method 1 ----
EXP     KMG(N), KOMP
        BAH,EXIT1
        D*(N), RLN2                     !1/LN2
        D+(U), E11
        ST(B,12,1), TEMEX, 128-12-11    !I as exponent
        SHFL,11
        *(N), LN2X                      !LN2X-11
        LX, $14, XW14
        ST(U), TEMPF
        D*(N), CONST($14)
DPLUS   D+(N), CONST+1.0($14)
        D*(N), TEMPF
        CB+, $14, DPLUS
        D+(N), CONST($14)
        E+(N), TEMEX
        B, 1.0($15)                     !normal return
EXIT1   C0011(BU,1),10.4,128-11         !exponent sign
        LA(U), $L                       !remove sign
        C1111(BU,1), $L, 127            !insert exponent flag
        B, 0.0($15)
! printed: KOMP DD(N), 1024*$N
KOMP    DD(N), 709.7827128933839968432456924
! printed: RLN2 DD(N), 1/$N
RLN2    DD(N), 1.442695040888963407359924681
! printed: E11 DD(N), 0X11
E11     DD(BU,64,8), (8)0005400000000000000000
! printed: LN2X DD(N), $NX-11
LN2X    DD(N), .6931471805599453094172321215X-11
XW14    XW,0,14,$
! printed: CONST DD(N), 1/13076743680000,1/87178291200
CONST   DD(N), 7.647163731819816475901131986E-14, 1.147074559772972471385169798E-11
! printed: DD(N), 1/6227020800, 1/479001600, 1/39916800
        DD(N), 1.605904383682161459939237717E-10, 2.087675698786809897921009032E-9, 2.505210838544171877505210839E-8
! printed: DD(N), 1/3628800, 1/362880, 1/40320, 1/5040, 1/720
        DD(N), 2.755731922398589065255731922E-7, 2.755731922398589065255731922E-6, 2.480158730158730158730158730E-5, 1.984126984126984126984126984E-4, 1.388888888888888888888888889E-3
! printed: DD(N), 1/120, 1/24, 1/6, 1/2, 1
        DD(N), 8.333333333333333333333333333E-3, 4.166666666666666666666666667E-2, 1.666666666666666666666666667E-1, .5, 1
TEMEX   DR(N), (1)
TEMPF   DR(N), (1)


        END, MAIN
